[
  {
    "name": "listCapabilities",
    "description": "Lists what this key may do. Call it first. Returns each collection and global the key can read or write, with whether it can create, publish, has drafts and exposes versions to findVersions, and a collection's \"idType\". Also returns the locales, the \"limits\" on page size and depth, and the enabled custom tools. Its \"server\" block holds the server version with repository and issue links, for a bug report.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {},
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "describeSchema",
    "description": "Describes the fields of a collection or global, one node at a time. Use it before a query or a write.\n\nWithout \"paths\" it returns the top-level node. A node has a \"schemaPath\", its \"fields\" and \"next\". Each field has a \"path\" relative to its node, a \"type\" and constraints such as \"required\", \"localized\", \"readOnly\", \"options\" and \"relationTo\". A \"blocks\" field lists the block slugs it accepts, and a \"richText\" field lists its node types in \"nodes\". \"next\" holds the schema paths of the blocks and rich text node types with fields below the node, e.g. \"/layout/sections/sectionWrapper\" or \"/content/block/callout\". Pass them as \"paths\" to describe those nodes. A block can accept different children at another position, so describe it at the schema path where it is used.\n\nWhen the response contains a rich text field, the response also carries a \"nodeProperties\" entry: the properties each node type must carry. Build every rich text node from it. Upload nodes have no schema path.\n\nid, _status, createdAt and updatedAt are not listed and cannot be written. A field marked \"readOnly\" cannot be written either.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "collection": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "pages",
            "posts",
            "tags",
            "notes",
            "snippets",
            "media"
          ]
        },
        "global": {
          "description": "Instead of \"collection\".",
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "site-settings",
            "banner"
          ]
        },
        "paths": {
          "description": "Schema paths from \"next\". Omit for the top-level node.",
          "maxItems": 400,
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "expand": {
          "description": "Return the top-level node and every node below it in one response, instead of \"paths\".",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "findDocuments",
    "description": "Finds documents in a collection. Returns one page of \"docs\" with paging totals. \"where\" is a Payload query, e.g. {\"title\":{\"contains\":\"home\"}}, with dots for nested fields, e.g. \"items.heading\". A \"where\" or \"sort\" on a hidden field, or through a relationship into a collection this key cannot read, is refused.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "collection": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "pages",
            "posts",
            "tags",
            "notes",
            "snippets",
            "media"
          ]
        },
        "where": {
          "type": "object",
          "propertyNames": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "additionalProperties": {}
        },
        "sort": {
          "description": "e.g. \"-updatedAt\" for descending.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Default 10.",
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 25
        },
        "page": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 9007199254740991
        },
        "depth": {
          "description": "Default 0. A relationship into a collection this key cannot read stays an id.",
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 1
        },
        "select": {
          "description": "Fields to return, e.g. {\"title\":true}.",
          "type": "object",
          "propertyNames": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "additionalProperties": {}
        },
        "locale": {
          "description": "Default: the default locale. A value missing in this locale is shown from the default locale.",
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "en",
            "de"
          ]
        },
        "draft": {
          "description": "Default true: latest drafts.",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "collection"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "getDocument",
    "description": "Reads one document or global, or with \"path\" only the value at that pointer. Returns the latest draft by default, with the \"updatedAt\" a write takes as \"expectedUpdatedAt\".\n\n\"versionId\" and \"diffFrom\" work where findVersions does. To revert, call getDocument with the old version as \"versionId\", the version findVersions marks \"latest\" as \"diffFrom\" and the locale you will write, then apply the returned \"patch\" with patchDocument.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "collection": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "pages",
            "posts",
            "tags",
            "notes",
            "snippets",
            "media"
          ]
        },
        "global": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "site-settings",
            "banner"
          ]
        },
        "id": {
          "description": "Required with \"collection\", omitted with \"global\".",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "number"
          ]
        },
        "path": {
          "description": "e.g. \"/layout/sections/0\".",
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^(\\/([^~/]|~[01])*)*$"
        },
        "depth": {
          "description": "Default 0. A relationship into a collection this key cannot read stays an id.",
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 1
        },
        "locale": {
          "description": "Default: the default locale. A value missing in this locale is shown from the default locale.",
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "en",
            "de"
          ]
        },
        "draft": {
          "description": "Default true. false reads the published version.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "outline": {
          "description": "With \"path\" at a rich text field: list each node's pointer, type, \"version\" and text.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "versionId": {
          "description": "From findVersions. Not with \"draft\".",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "number"
          ]
        },
        "diffFrom": {
          "description": "Version id, or \"published\" for the newest version published in any locale. Returns {from, to, patch}, the JSON Patch from that version to what is read.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "number"
          ]
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "findVersions",
    "description": "Lists the versions of one document or global, newest first, autosaves included. Returns per version \"versionId\", \"createdAt\", \"updatedAt\", \"status\", \"latest\", \"autosave\" and, where set, \"publishedLocale\", without the content. Read a version with getDocument \"versionId\", or compare it with \"diffFrom\".",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "collection": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "pages",
            "posts",
            "notes",
            "snippets",
            "media"
          ]
        },
        "global": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "site-settings"
          ]
        },
        "id": {
          "description": "Required with \"collection\", omitted with \"global\".",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "number"
          ]
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Default 10.",
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 25
        },
        "page": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 9007199254740991
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "published",
            "draft"
          ]
        },
        "locale": {
          "description": "Locale whose \"status\" is reported. Defaults to the default locale.",
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "en",
            "de"
          ]
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    }
  }
]
